# Copy to backend/.env and fill in the keys you have. Restart the API window after changes.
# Check what's switched on with:  .venv\Scripts\python.exe -m app.cli check
#
# Every outside service switches ON when its keys are set and stays OFF otherwise
# (nothing is faked):
#   no Google client ID  -> only phone sign-in is offered
#   no Twilio            -> (development only) the sign-in code is shown on screen
#   no Gemini/Anthropic  -> photos are shared with the tech but not analyzed
#   no Firebase          -> (development only) email links are shown on screen
#   no Stripe keys       -> no card needed; customers pay the shop directly

HVAC_ENVIRONMENT=dev                       # dev | prod
HVAC_DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./var/hvac.db
# Free hosted Postgres (Neon): paste the connection string as Neon shows it, or run
# scripts\windows\set-database.ps1:
# HVAC_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Created automatically by setup.ps1 / start-demo.ps1 (python -m app.cli secrets).
# HVAC_ENCRYPTION_KEY encrypts customer data in the database: back it up, never change it
# once there's data, and never commit it.
# HVAC_JWT_SECRET=
# HVAC_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Sign in with Google ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials > Create OAuth client ID > Web application.
# Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:8081 and http://localhost:5173
# (plus your real domains later). Paste the Client ID (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com).
# HVAC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS=1234567890-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com

# --- Email links (Firebase Authentication, free) ---------------------------------------------
# Proves shop sign-up emails and technician invites. Or run scripts\windows\set-firebase.ps1
# Firebase console > Authentication > Sign-in method > Email/Password ON, then
# Project settings > General > Web API key. (Free plan: 1,000 verification emails a day.)
# HVAC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIza...

# --- Phone sign-in codes + job texts (Twilio) --------------------------------------------
# Console > Verify > Services > create one, copy its SID (VA...).
# HVAC_TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=AC...
# HVAC_TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=...
# HVAC_TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=VA...
# Optional, for job-update texts (US numbers need A2P 10DLC registration):
# HVAC_TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+1...
# HVAC_TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=MG...

# --- Photo analysis -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FREE option: Google Gemini. Key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# (or run scripts\windows\set-gemini-key.ps1). Free tier has daily limits, and Google may
# use free-tier prompts to improve its products.
# HVAC_AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# HVAC_GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# Several keys, comma-separated, take turns (a key over its limit is skipped). Limits are
# per Google Cloud project, so create each key in a different project:
# HVAC_GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...one,AIza...two,AIza...three
# HVAC_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest
#
# Paid option: Claude. console.anthropic.com > API keys (needs credits)
# HVAC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# HVAC_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# --- Payments (Stripe) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# dashboard.stripe.com > Developers > API keys (use test keys first). Turn on Connect.
# HVAC_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# HVAC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# HVAC_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
HVAC_PLATFORM_FEE_BPS=1500                 # 15.00%

# --- Address lookup -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# census = free US Census Bureau geocoder, no key. Needs street, city, state and ZIP.
HVAC_GEOCODING_PROVIDER=census
# HVAC_GEOCODING_PROVIDER=google
# HVAC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=...

# --- URLs ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HVAC_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
HVAC_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=http://localhost:5173
